  "cil_liability": false,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed communication hub, by reason of its siting and design, would result in an unnecessary and harmful addition to street clutter within this section of the public footway, where similar structures already exist in close proximity. The cumulative impact of these features would detract from the established character of the High Street and diminish the quality of the public realm. The proposal is therefore contrary to London Plan Policy D8 (Public Realm), Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character) and CC5 (Advertisement Panels, Hoardings and Structures), and the aims of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed illuminated advertisement display sign with high illuminance level would introduce an incongruous addition which would harm the pedestrian experience along the street, and fail to preserve or enhance the character of the surrounding area. It will adversely impact the setting of the heritage asset and open space. Therefore, the proposal is contrary to Local Plan policies CC1, CC2 and CC5.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed communication hub, by reason of its siting and relationship with the approved highway works under planning permission ref. P/2025/0794, would result in unnecessary street clutter and would prejudice the delivery of agreed public realm and transport improvements. The proposal would therefore fail to preserve the quality, functionality and appearance of the public highway and is accordingly unacceptable. The development would therefore be contrary to Local Plan Policy EC2 (Developing a Sustainable Local Transport Network) and Policy CC5 (Advertisement Panels, Hoardings and Structures)."
  ]
